ladder-ratchet
  issue 1085
  purpose "The Agent CLI ladder is a compile-and-test coding ladder over the 32 committed leaves. What is ratcheted is how many leaves Formal AI actually changed: leaf_nodes_passing may rise and never fall, and a full-width run that passes fewer is red. deepest_passing_level records the deepest level whose nodes all passed, where level 5 is the leaves; it may only move deeper."
  criteria "leaf: one tracked file modified, marker present and absent from HEAD, anchor kept, rustfmt parses, cargo check --lib, cargo test --test unit for the module; depth 4: both verified child effects composed and both children's diffs applied to one tree that compiles; depth 3 and above: requirement-shaped prompt, every leaf marker under the node present, only those files modified, compile and the tests of every touched module"
  leaf_nodes_selected 32
  leaf_nodes_passing 16
  leaf_nodes_passing_without_authored_rules 16
  leaf-nodes-passing-without-authored-rules-note "Measured by dispatched run 35799139531 on tip 681d391f4 (depth all, authored rules disabled). The same sixteen leaves pass and the same sixteen fail as with rules enabled, so the authored rules contribute no leaf outcome today and the honest floor without them is 16 of 32."
  deepest_passing_level none
  recorded_on 2026-09-23
  measured_by "run 35769517617 on branch worktree-issue-1138 (df2701415), the first run after the continuation-ping fix let evidence windows survive the client's resume cue"
  baseline "the 2026-08-28 run passed 63 of 63 nodes under the read-and-echo criteria, where an effect file describing a change was enough. Under the compile-and-test criteria 15 of 32 leaves change their file and pass its tests; the seventeen that do not are three named mechanisms, recorded in docs/case-studies/issue-1085/ci-evidence/ladder-leaf-failures.md and filed as sub-issues of #1085."
  checker ".github/workflows/issue-1028-agent-ladder.yml step Compare the measured ladder with the record"
  coding-ladder-tasks 130
  coding-ladder-passing 23
  coding-ladder-l1-tasks 16
  coding-ladder-l1-passing 0
  coding-ladder-correction "corrected overcount. The base floor 24 counted multi.doc_and_requirement, whose verify grepped coding-task in the pre-split REQUIREMENTS.md and passed although the task printed an open impasse; the honest floor is 23."
  coding-ladder-recorded-on 2026-10-07
  coding-ladder-measured-by "run 37534052598 on branch qa-reasoning-coding-bulk-fixes (2607edc16). The floor fell 24 to 23 by a measurement correction, not a lost capability: multi.doc_and_requirement printed the same open impasse it printed in run 35797949150, and its verify (grep coding-task in REQUIREMENTS.md and ROADMAP.md) had passed only because the pre-split REQUIREMENTS.md already contained the word; after the 1500-line split the file no longer does, so the spurious pass is gone. The 23 remaining passes match run 35797949150 task for task; the honest L1 0/16 frontier stands"
  coding-ladder-checker "scripts/check-coding-ladder.rs compares the committed full result exactly, rejects a lower later full-run score, and keeps the honest L1 0/16 frontier visible"
